WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.059 --> 00:00:02.733
- Welcome back y'all.
We're here with Cher.

00:00:02.733 --> 00:00:03.566
Give it up.

00:00:03.566 --> 00:00:05.405
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.640
Her new Cher Decades Eau de Parfum

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:12.343
is available online and in
select retailers right now.

00:00:12.343 --> 00:00:14.360
Well, many people are obsessed with Cher

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.720
and understandably so, I am.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.376
But what is Cher obsessed with? Who knows.

00:00:19.376 --> 00:00:22.744
It's time to find out with
another round of Obsessions.

00:00:22.744 --> 00:00:25.032
(gentle whimsical music)
- [Announcer] Obsessions.

00:00:25.032 --> 00:00:27.928
(audience cheering)

00:00:27.928 --> 00:00:31.012
- So how this game
works is we hit a button

00:00:31.012 --> 00:00:34.705
on our super computer and it
will randomly select a topic

00:00:34.705 --> 00:00:37.912
either Cher or I obsess over.

00:00:37.912 --> 00:00:40.564
Then we have to really sell our obsession

00:00:40.564 --> 00:00:42.447
and why it's so great
and why we're into it.

00:00:42.447 --> 00:00:45.044
So since I'm not there, Marcel,

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:48.794
would you bring Cher our super computer.

00:00:48.794 --> 00:00:51.977
We're super rich. (laughs)

00:00:51.977 --> 00:00:52.810
Ooh, what?

00:00:54.074 --> 00:00:56.142
I've never seen that button.

00:00:56.142 --> 00:00:58.906
That's a, they gave you a
new whole bedazzled button.

00:00:58.906 --> 00:01:00.712
I love that. Okay, wait.

00:01:00.712 --> 00:01:02.842
I'm very impressed, art department.

00:01:02.842 --> 00:01:05.115
Okay so, Cher.
(audience clapping)

00:01:05.115 --> 00:01:07.703
So if you wouldn't mind
hitting that button on top

00:01:07.703 --> 00:01:09.060
because, well, I can't.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.268
- Okay.

00:01:10.268 --> 00:01:12.724
(roulette dinging)

00:01:12.724 --> 00:01:13.557
- [Kelly] It's a good button push.

00:01:13.557 --> 00:01:14.588
(roulette sharply dings)

00:01:14.588 --> 00:01:16.144
Oh, Bunnyville. Okay.

00:01:16.144 --> 00:01:20.534
Well it sounds like a houseman
went back in a Western film

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:22.677
but it's not. (laughs)

00:01:22.677 --> 00:01:25.636
Bunnyville, I have, me and my
kids, we have three bunnies

00:01:25.636 --> 00:01:27.480
and I'm obsessed right
now, 'cause I feel bad.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.270
Putting animals in cages bothers me a bit.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.113
So, I mean, I know you have
to sometimes, whatever,

00:01:32.113 --> 00:01:35.218
but like, so I'm building
in my backyard, like,

00:01:35.218 --> 00:01:36.522
I call it Bunnyville.

00:01:36.522 --> 00:01:37.747
It's ridiculous.

00:01:37.747 --> 00:01:40.702
It's like they have their
own little theme park

00:01:40.702 --> 00:01:43.263
in my backyard and there's
just three bunnies,

00:01:43.263 --> 00:01:45.307
so I'm obsessed with them. (laughs)

00:01:45.307 --> 00:01:47.742
(audience applauding)

00:01:47.742 --> 00:01:50.057
Do you like, do you have any animals?

00:01:50.057 --> 00:01:52.841
- Well, I rescued an elephant in Islamabad

00:01:52.841 --> 00:01:55.313
and took him to Cambodia.
(audience applauding)

00:01:55.313 --> 00:01:58.420
- Way to trump me with that. Wait, what?

00:01:58.420 --> 00:01:59.481
(laughs) Like, what?

00:01:59.481 --> 00:02:01.689
That's incredible. That's so cool.

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:03.725
- I know. It's happened on Twitter.

00:02:03.725 --> 00:02:05.887
I got all these kids
saying, "Save Kaavan,"

00:02:05.887 --> 00:02:07.151
hashtag whatever.

00:02:07.151 --> 00:02:08.696
And so I start
(audience chuckling)

00:02:08.696 --> 00:02:11.624
and I thought, I'm like, I'm
gonna go save a elephant,

00:02:11.624 --> 00:02:13.221
I'm just a singer, you know?

00:02:13.221 --> 00:02:16.978
So we started fighting
and it took us four years,

00:02:16.978 --> 00:02:19.450
and then I think that they knew something.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.576
They said, "Okay, you can have him

00:02:21.576 --> 00:02:23.626
but only if Cher picks him up."

00:02:23.626 --> 00:02:27.790
So obviously they don't know me. So, yeah.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:29.022
- (laughs) They didn't
think you'd show up.

00:02:29.022 --> 00:02:32.184
- Uh-uh. I showed up,
I showed up big time.

00:02:32.184 --> 00:02:35.242
And then we brought him,
and he's so beautiful,

00:02:35.242 --> 00:02:36.630
then we brought him to Cambodia.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.694
- It's a really cool thing that,
especially people with you,

00:02:39.694 --> 00:02:41.879
it's just a giant spotlight,

00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:44.253
highlight that and actually make change.

00:02:44.253 --> 00:02:46.019
But now it's your turn, Cher.

00:02:46.019 --> 00:02:49.157
So you press the button for you.

00:02:49.157 --> 00:02:51.836
- [Announcer] Obsessions.
(roulette dinging)

00:02:51.836 --> 00:02:52.669
(roulette sharply dings)

00:02:52.669 --> 00:02:55.175
(audience wooing)

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.008
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:02:56.008 --> 00:02:56.841
- Okay.

00:02:57.841 --> 00:02:59.458
- Elvis?

00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:00.652
- Yeah, when I was 10 years old

00:03:00.652 --> 00:03:03.205
my mom took me to the
Pan Pacific to see Elvis.

00:03:03.205 --> 00:03:05.203
I just, I really loved him.

00:03:05.203 --> 00:03:07.974
And then when I got older,

00:03:07.974 --> 00:03:12.224
not this old but older, he
invited me to Las Vegas.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:17.760
(audience wooing)
- He what?

00:03:18.957 --> 00:03:22.657
- One of his people
called, close your mouth.

00:03:22.657 --> 00:03:24.713
(audience laughing)
One of his people,

00:03:24.713 --> 00:03:26.610
one of his people called and said,

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.965
"Would you like to come
up for the weekend?"

00:03:28.965 --> 00:03:32.193
And I was so terrified
that I couldn't do it.

00:03:32.193 --> 00:03:34.183
(audience oohing)
Oh, shut up. (laughs)

00:03:34.183 --> 00:03:35.792
- What?

00:03:35.792 --> 00:03:37.913
When Elvis says, "Let's hang out,"

00:03:37.913 --> 00:03:39.971
just, you go for the story.

00:03:39.971 --> 00:03:42.795
- Right, but it was, he was on
the other side of, you know,

00:03:42.795 --> 00:03:44.956
he was on the downside of himself, so.

00:03:44.956 --> 00:03:46.225
(audience laughing)
- Oh.

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:47.962
- And I don't mean like,
handsome, whatever, like that,

00:03:47.962 --> 00:03:51.495
but he was on the downside of
the drugs and stuff like that.

00:03:51.495 --> 00:03:52.739
- That was maybe a smart decision.

00:03:52.739 --> 00:03:54.693
Okay. Okay.
- Yeah.

00:03:54.693 --> 00:03:55.526
- That was a really good obsession.

00:03:55.526 --> 00:03:58.087
- Right, you don't wanna get
involved with another musician

00:03:58.087 --> 00:04:00.059
who does drugs, I did that.

00:04:00.059 --> 00:04:02.039
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. That's not fun.

00:04:02.039 --> 00:04:05.549
So everybody, I can't
believe we ended with Elvis.

00:04:05.549 --> 00:04:07.386
That was incredible, Cher.

00:04:07.386 --> 00:04:09.411
Those are our obsessions.

00:04:09.411 --> 00:04:11.222
(gentle whimsical music)
- [Announcer] Obsessions.

00:04:11.222 --> 00:04:14.334
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:16.647
- Well, everyone be sure to go

00:04:16.647 --> 00:04:18.680
and get Cher's new fragrance collection.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:20.427
I promise you they smell really good.

00:04:20.427 --> 00:04:23.091
It's called Cher Decades Eau de Parfum.

00:04:23.091 --> 00:04:24.501
And it's available online

00:04:24.501 --> 00:04:26.436
and also in select retailers right now.

